### Observation 3: Persona Avatar & Static Asset Path Resolution Across Ports (:3011 vs :80)

**Status:** APPLIED
**Date:** 2026-09-16
**Session context:** Full-window chatbot header avatar image repair
**Skill:** task-observer
**Type:** user-feedback
**Phase/Area:** Static Hosting & Asset Resolution

**Issue:** When viewing the full-page chatbot on `:3011`, the header avatar image (`/chat/persona/face-icon.png`) returned 404 because `static/chat/persona` was not present in `:3011`'s document root, whereas on `:80` it was routed to `/volume1/web/chat/persona/`.

**Applied Solutions:**
1. **Document Root Symlinking**: Linked `/volume1/homes/me/services/chatbot-data/persona` to `static/chat/persona` and `static/persona` inside `services/chatbot/`.
2. **Server-Side Routing & MIME Normalization (`server.py`)**: Added dedicated persona route and enabled accurate MIME type guessing (`image/png`) for static files.
3. **Cache-Buster & Nginx Fallback**: Appended `?v=2` to prevent cached 404s and provided an `onerror` handler falling back to port 80 nginx (`//location.hostname/chat/persona/face-icon.png`).

**Principle:** Microservice web frontends on non-standard ports must symlink shared static asset trees into their local static roots and provide port-agnostic `onerror` fallbacks to canonical web endpoints.

